From: Fractal Microsystems <maintainers@fractalmicro.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] compiler: recognize GCC 15 with the existing port attributes

The historical port supplies a GCC 14 compatibility header. GCC 15.3 uses
the same attribute definitions for this build; retain that contract rather
than adding a second copy. The compiler dialect is pinned to GNU89 by the
recipe. This is a bridge to a newer U-Boot port, not general GCC support.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [historical downstream port]

diff --git a/include/linux/compiler-gcc15.h b/include/linux/compiler-gcc15.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/linux/compiler-gcc15.h
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+/* GCC 15.3: retain the port's existing compiler attribute contract. */
+#include <linux/compiler-gcc14.h>
